<title>JAPAN: Japan 20-yr bond auction lowest price 99.50.</title>
<headline>Japan 20-yr bond auction lowest price 99.50.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tuesday's auction of 400 billion yen worth of 3.1 percent 20-year Japanese government bonds produced the following  results, the Ministry of Finance said:</p>
<p>Lowest price	  99.50    Stop rate	   3.140 pct</p>
<p>Average price	 99.57    Average yield     3.134 pct</p>
<p>Total bids	   981.3 billion yen</p>
<p>Accepted Bids	398.8 billion yen</p>
<p>Bids accepted at lowest price 70.8201 pct</p>
<p>Issue date    July 22, 1997   Maturity    Sept 20, 2017</p>
</text>
